briefing 0.3.1 (Getty/briefing 4e139b7, 6fb3d9a; briefing karr #1/#2, both done) settled where Codex agents declare their skills: a comment line in the agent TOML, because Codex 0.153 deserializes agent role files with deny_unknown_fields and drops the whole role over a [briefing] table ("unknown field `briefing`").

    name = "my_agent"
    description = "..."
    # briefing: skills = ["getty-perl-core", "superpowers:brainstorming"]
    developer_instructions = """
    ...
    """

Rules from the hook (hooks/briefing-preload, parse_skills_comment):
- one line, `# briefing: skills = [ ... ]`, items as double- or single-quoted strings;
- must sit OUTSIDE any multi-line string — a matching line inside developer_instructions is prose and is ignored;
- first match wins; a leftover [briefing] table is still read (with a migration systemMessage), but must not be emitted.

Verified live on Codex 0.153.4 with a control agent, including a role whose file name differs from its `name`, a spawn from a repo subdirectory, and a role declared via [agents.<name>] config_file. The hook finds agents by the `name` field and honours CODEX_HOME, so skilletor's `agents/<name>.toml` with `name = data.name || itemName` is fine either way.

